1
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:21,330
you stop?

2
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:30,800
Shut it up!

3
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:30,950
WaaaaaaaAAAAH.

4
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:44,255
AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAH.

5
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:47,540
Ufff...the whole island
floating in the sky.

6
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:49,395
This is like a dream.

7
00:01:50,260 --> 00:01:51,090
no...

8
00:01:51,173 --> 00:01:52,003
A NIGHMARE!

9
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:56,880
How can we hope it to be Kaido
His strength is too great!

10
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,110
What?

11
00:01:59,193 --> 00:02:00,820
Why are you here?

12
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:01,980
No way!

13
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:06,180
Marco the Phoenix!

14
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:08,640
We need a lot of fire now!

15
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:10,080
Easy enough.

16
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:12,280
In that case, here you go.

17
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:17,700
What are you doing?

18
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:18,937
Oh, no, it's hot!

19
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:19,850
It's so hot!

20
00:02:19,933 --> 00:02:21,177
I'm burning from the inside out!

21
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:22,090
Damn it!

22
00:02:22,173 --> 00:02:23,917
Is this some kind of joke to you?

23
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,941
Thought you were an ally,
and this is what you do?

24
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:29,460
Explain yourself, or die!

25
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:35,840
Boy, somebody has a real short fuse.

26
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,617
All right, don't worry, Chopper.

27
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:41,112
I'll put it out for you.

28
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:44,480
Oh, my arm bones! I'm burning!

29
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:46,700
Or not.

30
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:48,460
Well, this is unique.

31
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:50,757
It's all right, my friend.

32
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:51,670
Relax.

33
00:02:51,753 --> 00:02:52,900
But the fire!

34
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:54,570
Oh, wait.

35
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:56,420
Uh, I'm not burning.

36
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:57,820
I'm totally okay.

37
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:01,260
It's warm and comfy like
a perfect summer day.

38
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:04,260
It feels so nice. Dr. Chopper!

39
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:08,017
We're ready to begin
production of the antibodies.

40
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:09,982
If you girl would come this way!

41
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:14,200
Oh, my goodness!

42
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:15,980
It's a swarm of ice, Oni!

43
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:19,380
Miyagi, Tristan, run for it, hurry!

44
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:22,358
Might as well get them all, I guess.

45
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:27,720
Phoenix Pyrapples!

46
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:40,860
Wait, this is kind of nice, actually.

47
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,340
I can feel the chill melting away already.

48
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:51,230
Ah!

49
00:03:51,313 --> 00:03:52,420
What was I doing?

50
00:03:53,220 --> 00:03:54,320
Are you alright?

51
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:58,626
You had me worried there, but it
seems you came to your senses.

52
00:03:59,420 --> 00:04:01,160
You sure scared me!

53
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:05,397
That's nice, but only thing I did
was raise their body temperature.

54
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:09,777
The second their stamina runs out, they'll
start going berserk just like before.

55
00:04:09,860 --> 00:04:12,978
So you better use the time
while you've still got it.

56
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:17,620
You're a lifesaver!

57
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:20,420
A little time is all I needed.

58
00:04:21,420 --> 00:04:22,760
Tristan! Miyagi!

59
00:04:23,380 --> 00:04:25,100
You okay over there?

60
00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:28,180
Yes, it seems.

61
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:30,717
Just shaking up is all. All right, then.

62
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,200
Let's get down to it.

63
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:35,497
Since we're clear for now,
we'll get right to work.

64
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:36,640
Thanks a bunch.

65
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:39,217
Guess they're using space in that tower.

66
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:40,130
Okay?

67
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,500
I'll kill you.

68
00:04:44,760 --> 00:04:48,957
stupid bird and stupid raccoon playing
doctor and messing up all my stuff.

69
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:50,657
hey, you morons!

70
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:53,437
you don't really think he's gonna
spare his own enemies, do you?

71
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:56,997
he's gonna save his buddies and
they're gonna finish you off.

72
00:04:57,080 --> 00:05:01,397
i don't know, our friends
are gonna die, that's right.

73
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:02,310
they'll die.

74
00:05:02,393 --> 00:05:05,577
then you're all gonna
die unless you get rid of

75
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:08,542
that pest and bring back
my antibody immediately.

76
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:10,040
Simple enough.

77
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:14,377
I can lend a hand without much effort,
but it seems like we're overstaffed.

78
00:05:14,460 --> 00:05:15,640
Roronoa, listen up.

79
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:19,959
I think you might be better off
fighting Kaido on the roof right now.

80
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:23,137
Having trouble getting up there?

81
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:24,867
Why not let me fly you then?

82
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:29,791
You Straw Hats are way too strong to
be dealing with a bunch of small fries.

83
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:32,200
But we can't leave yet.

84
00:05:32,340 --> 00:05:34,281
We still have to protect Chopper.

85
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:38,740
It's fine, Mr.

86
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:43,400
Skeleton We can handle this We
won't let any harm come to Mr.

87
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:45,120
Raccoon You have my word.

88
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:50,577
Let's give it our best.

89
00:05:50,660 --> 00:05:51,640
We've got this.

90
00:05:57,320 --> 00:05:58,177
Hold up.

91
00:05:58,260 --> 00:06:00,060
I'm not done with you yet.

92
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:03,580
A poo.

93
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:06,040
Check it!

94
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:10,060
You punks better give me
back that antibody or else!

95
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:15,460
They'll kill me if I don't get it!

96
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:16,740
I can't lose now!

97
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:18,880
I'm fighting for my life, dammit!

98
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:20,620
Oh, seriously?

99
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:21,990
Very well.

100
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:22,980
Have at you.

101
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:24,340
One more enemy.

102
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:26,151
Then we'll be on our way.

103
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:29,677
Flee to the tower, Mr. Raccoon!

104
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:30,701
We're all right!

105
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:45,050
Nooo!

106
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:46,800
Nooooo! Nooooo!

107
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:52,060
That's new.

108
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:53,700
He betrayed us?

109
00:06:53,860 --> 00:06:56,497
So does that mean we should
attack him to protect Apoo?

110
00:06:56,580 --> 00:06:57,410
Noooo!

111
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:01,560
Noooo! Noooo!

112
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:03,690
That's new.

113
00:07:04,460 --> 00:07:09,840
Roronoa Zoro, if you can trust me as your
ally, let me handle this and go ahead.

114
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:14,134
Well, if nothing else,

115
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:18,005
it looks like you've got a knack
for betting on the right horse.

116
00:07:19,560 --> 00:07:20,437
Hey, Saji!

117
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:21,440
Where are you?

118
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:23,260
If I had to guess,

119
00:07:23,620 --> 00:07:26,337
I'd wager that he sensed
a powerful enemy nearby,

120
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:28,377
and he's holding them
off on the third floor.

121
00:07:28,460 --> 00:07:29,777
I didn't think of that.

122
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:32,037
Guess my observation hockey's still weak.

123
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:35,840
He can't be far from here, but
I can't sense Sanji at all!

124
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:42,920
Do you feel something just now, enemies?

125
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:45,810
Indeed.

126
00:07:45,893 --> 00:07:46,723
Many of them.

127
00:07:46,806 --> 00:07:48,820
Nearby, ready to strike.

128
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:51,891
It seems they're quite formidable as well.

129
00:07:57,940 --> 00:08:02,116
One of us is going to have to stay
behind and keep these foes occupied.

130
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:05,100
You go on ahead.

131
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:06,929
I'll draw their attention.

132
00:08:08,420 --> 00:08:10,060
Up and load!

133
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:13,490
General...

134
00:08:13,573 --> 00:08:14,780
Launcher!

135
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:30,460
Now that is how you make a mess of things!

136
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:33,160
CENRAL TANON!

137
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:35,940
Damn it! Get back!

138
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:42,810
Huh?

139
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:48,940
You think I'm just gonna
let you blow everything up?

140
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:53,460
Don't push it, little robot!

141
00:08:55,380 --> 00:08:58,027
Wow, that is one hell
of an upgrade, brother!

142
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:05,440
I love being good, Dinosaur!

143
00:09:09,180 --> 00:09:11,740
The Triceratops, huh? What of it?

144
00:09:11,980 --> 00:09:15,156
Dinosaurs are the strongest
creatures that ever lived.

145
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:19,400
You're gonna get scrapped,
you giant tin can!

146
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:21,660
Who are you calling a tin can?

147
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:24,720
Waffle Metal never loses its luster!

148
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:44,120
It's the Tobi Rupal! No!

149
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:55,780
Little pests, where did they go?

150
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:59,440
I'm ever, ever so cross, brother dear.

151
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:04,580
Why, I just might crush that bitch's
head into a thousand little pieces.

152
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:21,420
follow him that way i'm
here what's the big hurry

153
00:10:25,020 --> 00:10:30,837
damn it what is this get
this crap off me don't tire

154
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:36,100
yourself out already after
all the fun's just starting

155
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:44,420
are you a gentleman or not you
said you loved me was that a lie

156
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:58,237
i've been looking for a cute pet like
you i think i just might keep you

157
00:10:58,320 --> 00:11:04,500
forever i already told you i have to
go my captain is counting on me and yet

158
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:12,760
there's women everywhere i
look ladies ladies ladies

159
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:21,877
could this be heaven i
think the man's lost his

160
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:25,760
mind yes well he's lucky
he's still good looking

161
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:33,217
of course Straw Hat and his
crew managed to break through

162
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:37,760
our forces that's no good
for kaido this is a real mess

163
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:45,880
could you hold on for a sec i don't
like you picking on my underlay

164
00:11:50,620 --> 00:11:52,957
i thought a former warlord would show some

165
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:55,637
restraint but you came
out swinging like a common

166
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:59,237
thug i'll have you know
i'm the helmsman of

167
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:01,897
the Straw Hat pirates
now if you want to speak

168
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:04,997
of manners then use my
proper title my mistake

169
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:08,217
it has been a while but
i saw you when you were

170
00:12:08,300 --> 00:12:13,477
a warlord so that stuck
with me you what well

171
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:17,340
enough about all that
out with it who are you

172
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:20,640
Who indeed, I do wonder.

173
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:23,260
I'll find out soon either way.

174
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:25,840
After I tear off that mask.

175
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:29,680
Not that easy, pal.

176
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:40,400
I doubt anyone will come
here, so we can hide at least.

177
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:43,700
Do you know what this is?

178
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:45,337
A statue of a dragon.

179
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:48,057
It used to be at the
entrance of the island,

180
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:51,081
but my friend broke it,
so they tossed it in here.

181
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:52,500
Your friend?

182
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:54,330
Yes.

183
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:56,300
Several years ago.

184
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:59,929
He came here in hopes
of killing my father.

185
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:10,540
That's weird.

186
00:13:10,880 --> 00:13:11,720
No one's here.

187
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:16,830
Aaaaaaahhh!

188
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,000
Intruder alert!

189
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:26,600
I'm here for Kaido, not for you!

190
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:33,980
What now, Ace?

191
00:13:34,220 --> 00:13:35,060
I got this!

192
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:38,560
You guys save the kids! On it! Good luck!

193
00:13:41,660 --> 00:13:43,366
You're persistent, aren't ya?

194
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:50,217
Who the hell are you?

195
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:51,477
Tell me your name.

196
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:53,620
You tell me yours.

197
00:13:57,920 --> 00:14:02,300
My name's Ace and I'm not
leaving till I take Kaido's hand.

198
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:07,320
I found them over here. Hurry.

199
00:14:09,460 --> 00:14:10,497
Don't be afraid.

200
00:14:10,580 --> 00:14:12,397
We came here to rescue you.

201
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:13,310
Come on.

202
00:14:13,393 --> 00:14:14,909
Let's get you out of here.

203
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:25,240
You're pretty strong.

204
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,030
Ace!

205
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:34,040
We have the kids with us. Everyone's okay.

206
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:37,557
But the bad news is there's no
sign of Kaido anywhere here.

207
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:38,470
What?

208
00:14:38,553 --> 00:14:40,380
My father is off on an expedition.

209
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:44,500
And not only him, his
officers are gone too.

210
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:45,890
Your father?

211
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:51,358
So Kaido has a daughter, and he left
her in charge of the whole place?

212
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,340
I am Yamato!

213
00:14:54,820 --> 00:14:58,232
Now I think it's time we all
stop this pointless violence.

214
00:14:58,340 --> 00:15:00,458
If you have time to wonder who I am,

215
00:15:00,620 --> 00:15:04,914
get out of here right now and take
those children back to their families!

216
00:15:06,180 --> 00:15:08,060
I'd be happy to do just that.

217
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:11,097
But will Kaido forgive
you for letting us go?

218
00:15:11,180 --> 00:15:14,760
I have no obligation to
protect this island for him.

219
00:15:24,220 --> 00:15:25,050
Ready?

220
00:15:25,133 --> 00:15:26,937
We'll have you back home in no time.

221
00:15:27,020 --> 00:15:27,850
Don't worry.

222
00:15:27,933 --> 00:15:29,457
Your families are waiting for you.

223
00:15:29,540 --> 00:15:31,900
Of course. Thank you. Thank you.

224
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:33,237
I mean it.

225
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:35,177
Are you sure you want to stay here, Ace?

226
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:38,157
We're heading back to the mainland,
so you'll be on your own for now.

227
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:39,070
It's fine.

228
00:15:39,153 --> 00:15:40,317
Better to get those kids home.

229
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:42,282
I'll catch up to you guys later.

230
00:15:47,220 --> 00:15:48,697
You say you're not a captain,

231
00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:52,057
but there's no way someone as strong
as you would just hang around here!

232
00:15:52,140 --> 00:15:53,660
Give me your worst.

233
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:55,720
You want to fight that fight?

234
00:15:56,020 --> 00:15:57,420
I was bored anyway

235
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:32,477
Something's up.

236
00:16:32,560 --> 00:16:36,089
If you're this strong, then why
aren't you going out to sea?

237
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:38,760
It's his fault that I'm stuck here.

238
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:40,630
Kaido.

239
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:44,000
All because I was born his child.

240
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:45,730
Oh, really?

241
00:16:45,900 --> 00:16:47,782
So it's all your father's fault?

242
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:50,680
Aren't you just making excuses?

243
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:57,296
Everyone's the same.

244
00:16:58,400 --> 00:17:00,480
We can't choose our parents.

245
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:01,759
You gotta make do.

246
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:04,240
Do you think I'm stupid?

247
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:06,544
You don't have to tell me that!

248
00:17:07,120 --> 00:17:09,160
You say you get it, but do you?

249
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:13,077
You hate your father, but
you've given him power.

250
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:14,454
He chained your hands.

251
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:18,034
But right now, you're letting
him chain your heart, too.

252
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:20,310
Huh?

253
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:40,160
Yamato, why don't you tell
me what you really want?

254
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:15,260
I understand now.

255
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:19,398
Somewhere in my heart, I've
been holding myself back.

256
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,960
Before I knew it, I was
afraid to even say it.

257
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:26,340
That I want to sail the
world on a grand adventure!

258
00:18:26,700 --> 00:18:29,759
That I want to be like Odin
and live my life freely!

259
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:32,277
I'll go...

260
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:33,460
to the sea.

261
00:18:34,180 --> 00:18:36,340
I'll find a way off this island.

262
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:40,140
I'll find a way to be free
just like I always dreamed!

263
00:18:43,860 --> 00:18:45,801
Yeah, now you're talking, Yamato.

264
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:00,920
Much better.

265
00:19:02,700 --> 00:19:04,641
Did that clear things up for you?

266
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:21,040
And he came home all busted up again.

267
00:19:22,420 --> 00:19:25,657
I laugh, but he really gave me a
lot of trouble when we were kids.

268
00:19:25,740 --> 00:19:26,617
That little dope.

269
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:30,200
Your brother sounds like
so much fun. Hell yeah!

270
00:19:31,180 --> 00:19:33,397
So, who are the top pirates right now?

271
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:37,127
Is anyone our age making a name
for themselves people our age?

272
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:42,837
Let me think well the girls are crazy
for some cabin something guy Oh, yeah.

273
00:19:42,920 --> 00:19:45,357
Well, nobody is on my level just yet.

274
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:49,837
But each C has their own tough guy and one
of them just might make it big someday.

275
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:51,240
like who like who?

276
00:19:51,460 --> 00:19:56,240
Kid in the south blue and law in
the north and veggie in the west.

277
